<title>PHILIPPINES: Sales of Philippine export zones up 46.61 pct.</title>
<headline>Sales of Philippine export zones up 46.61 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of companies within special export zones went up by 46.61 percent to $3.979 billion in the first eight months of the year as compared with $2.714 billion in the same period last year, the Philippine Economic Zone Authority said on Monday.</p>
<p>Leading the list is the Philippine unit of Texas Instruments with total export sales amounting to $793.749 million.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
